From f1b2c21704460aef9183179d66db84a2a70da08d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cline <cline@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:09:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] ci(release): clean up the publishing job

- Drop the second 'Checkout repository' step. It ran after the toolchain
  install and re-checked out a tree that was already current.
- Move the binutils install ahead of the build (it used to run after it) and
  then remove it entirely: it existed only to provide a cross 'strip' for
  before_deploy.sh, which nothing invoked. Cargo already strips the release
  binary via the 'strip = true' profile setting.
- Replace MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET 10.7 with 10.13. 10.7 is below the floor of
  every currently supported Rust target and is silently ignored on the musl,
  ARM and Windows runners it was applied to.
- Declare permissions: contents: write explicitly instead of relying on the
  repository default token scope.
- Delete the orphaned .github/workflows/before_deploy.sh. The packaging step
  claimed it 'will run automatically on release builds'; no workflow has ever
  referenced it. It was also the only thing that built .deb packages and wrote
  archives to the repository root, which is what the original upload glob
  expected -- the inline replacement moved the archives into artifacts/ and
  did not update the glob.
- Drop the now-dead 'ia-get*.deb' upload pattern, the stale '--features gui'
  comments (the GUI was deleted in 2.1.0) and the hardcoded Gameaday/ia-get-cli
  release URLs (use github.repository).
